{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778952274,"nonce":"+6MAM5EGlUOORJ9bxyrl+nAMbYs=","title":"Use shared series loader for RSS, search, and sitemap","message":"## Problem\nGenerated discovery surfaces are missing or mislabeling series content.\n\nCurrent evidence:\n- `scripts/generate-rss.mjs` looks for `_series.json`; current series metadata lives in `_series.md`, so the build reported `Found 0 series posts`.\n- `scripts/generate-search-index.mjs` also looks for `_series.json`; the generated `public/search/index.json` had zero `/series/` entries after build.\n- `app/sitemap.ts` only emits `/`, `/blog`, and regular blog posts; it omits `/verse`, `/series`, series detail pages, and series posts.\n\n## Context\nThe main site renderer already has working `lib/series.ts` helpers for `_series.md`. The scripts duplicate older series-loading logic, so they have drifted from the real content model.\n\n## Potential Solutions\n- Make RSS/search generation consume the same series loader semantics as the app, or factor a build-safe shared content loader.\n- Include series index, series pages, series posts, and verse in the sitemap.\n- Add a build assertion or small test that generated search/RSS include at least one known non-draft series post when series content exists.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}